      "writtenOn": "2022-12-15T18:01:27Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "The way we deal with these situations is typically by mapping the error to one of the existing values. For example, the CString errors would be mapped to `ERROR_OOM` or `IO` (just like the library would do internally).\n\nAnd this raises a good point: the `map_err` here shouldn\u0027t blindly return `PayloadVerificationError`. Instead, we should `match` the result and only return `VerificationError` when that was the case, other results (such as `ERROR_IO` or `OOM`) should result in `InternalError`. Furthermore, I\u0027d say that `AVB_SLOT_VERIFY_RESULT_ERROR_PUBLIC_KEY_REJECTED` deserves its own `RebootReason`.",
      "parentUuid": "f6ec4061_29fa35d0",
